# A mode whose target can't be chosen can't be chosen (CR 700.2a, 603.3c): Bot2 controls no permanent, so Deceiver Exarch's
# "Tap target permanent an opponent controls" is no choice, and with one mode left Bot1 is asked none (the refusal); the trigger
# is "Untap target permanent you control". Its target, the first Bot1 controls (the refusal holds the script's cursor, so the
# target is the default), is the Island Bot1 tapped to cast the Exarch: it untaps and taps for {U} again, beside the {U} left
# from the Lotus (were the target the Exarch, the Island would still be tapped). The sibling scenarios, with a permanent of
# Bot2's out, are asked the mode.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Black Lotus
Deceiver Exarch
Island x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x15

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Hand.Deceiver Exarch.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
! Bot1.Modes
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
? Bot1.Mana = {U}{U}

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Island; Deceiver Exarch
Bot2.Battlefield.Count = 0
Bot1.Graveyard = Black Lotus
